Alicia: Quick help — AtlasBank POC needs a Rust streaming SDK example + tool/function-calling for structured payment JSON. They're hitting auth + corporate proxy issues; also pricing and security Qs. Can someone own?

Sam: I'll take this. Are they on hosted or dedicated right now? @alicia_sales

Alicia: Hosted for POC (may move to Dedicated). Need: 1) Rust SSE/websocket streaming sample, 2) example of tool/function calls that return structured JSON we can parse, 3) ephemeral creds / short-lived tokens + IP allowlist, 4) pricing estimate for spikes ~1k TPS, 5) answers for KMS and SOC2. Blocker: our Rust SDK fails behind their MITM TLS proxy — handshake errors.

Maya: Dropping a tiny Rust snippet for streaming + simple parse. This uses tokio + async-tungstenite pattern — swap to your fav crate if needed.

```
// minimal async streaming pseudocode
use tokio_tungstenite::connect_async;
use futures_util::{StreamExt, SinkExt};

async fn run() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let (mut ws, _resp) = connect_async("wss://api.redwood.ai/v1/stream?model=rl-medium").await?;
  ws.send("{\"input\": \"pay 100 to acct 123\"}").await?;
  while let Some(msg) = ws.next().await { println!("recv: {:?}", msg?); }
  Ok(())
}
```

Maya: For structured tool calls, set the response format to our func-json variant and parse like:

```
{"tool": "charge_card", "args": {"amount_cents": 10000, "currency": "USD"}}
```

Sam: Implementation notes — in the SDK set `response_format: "func-json"` and then validate payloads with your proto/json-schema. Example: `resp.parse::<ToolCall>()`.

Jordan: Proxy note — if the bank is terminating TLS for inspection, you will see handshake failures from native TLS stacks. Options:
- Ask Atlas to allow egress to our dedicated IPs (IP allowlist)
- Use mutual TLS with client certs (we can provision per-customer certs for Dedicated or Private)
- For POC only: use our proxy opt-in flag to accept upstream proxy certs (not recommended for prod)

Nina: KMS/Security — hosted uses HSM-backed keys (AWS KMS/CloudHSM) by default. For Dedicated/Private we support BYOK and on-prem HSM with audit logs. We have SOC 2 Type II + ISO docs; I'll post the SOC2 packet link: https://redwood.example.com/security/soc2

Kevin: Pricing quick take — for the POC we can offer 90 days trial credits. Rough order of magnitude: hosted bursty spikes (1k TPS, short lived) ~ $15k–$30k/month depending on token sizes; Dedicated reserved commit (SLA + steady 1k TPS) ballpark $45k–$80k/month. We can model a detailed estimate once we know avg tokens/response and concurrency.

Alicia: Thanks — scheduling sync with Atlas infra tomorrow 10am PT. @sam_presales @maya_se can you join? I'll send calendar invite and add a checklist: certs, IPs, sample runbook.

Sam: Yep — joining.

